.TH AGENT 1
.SH NAME
agent \- run a reusable filesystem worker through public Bench tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B agent run
[options] [DEFINITION] [--] [GOAL ...]
.br
.B agent tick
[options] [DEFINITION]
.br
.B agent check
[path options] DEFINITION
.br
.B agent show
[path options] DEFINITION
.SH DESCRIPTION
Agent validates the definition, compiles private context, and invokes Ply.
The original bin/check decides completion. Agent does not implement a model loop.
Use agent help for the full option list.
.SH INPUT PROTECTION
.TP
.BI \-read-only " PATH"
Protect an existing file or directory through Cage. Repeat for up to 128 distinct
paths. Relative paths resolve from the caller's directory.
.TP
.B \-protect-inputs
Protect existing WORK/inputs and WORK/request.md. Missing conventional paths are
skipped. Explicit paths must exist. Symlinks and multiply-linked files are refused.
.PP
Protection confines actions, checks and heartbeat wakes to workspace, state and
private temporary writes. Protected paths are excluded. Networking requires
-net; reads remain unrestricted. Checks needing other writable locations must be
adapted. A private controller-owned invocation file freezes the selections and
is recorded. A boundary setup failure stops with 125 before caller runtime writes.
.PP
AGENT_PROTECT_INPUTS=1 requires protection. It cannot be disabled by
-protect-inputs=false or -no-cage. Protection is not a snapshot and cannot prevent
another host process or inherited writable descriptor from changing input bytes.
.SH OUTCOMES
Ply's exit status is preserved: 0 checked, 1 broken, 2 unfinished, 3 declined,
75 parked, 125 boundary or recording failure, 130 interrupted.
Definition and invocation failures use 1 and 2 respectively.
.SH SEE ALSO
Agent README.md, RUNNER.md, SECURITY.md; ply(1), cage(1), record(1).
